      "math_academy_id": "q-16565",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d58fba3c-4bbf-5a74-a911-18db101eb632",
      "knowledge_point": "Determining the Center and Axis Lengths Given a Homogeneous Polynomial Equation of an Ellipse",
      "problem": "Determine the length of the major axis of the ellipse whose equation is ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+10x-16y+25=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we must group the $x$ terms and the $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+10x-16y+25 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+10x)+(4{y}^{2}-16y)+25 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we complete the square for both the $x$ and $y$ terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}+10x)+(4{y}^{2}-16y)+25 & =0 \\\\ [{x}^{2}+10x]+4[{y}^{2}-4y]+25 & =0 \\\\ [(x+5)^{2}-{5}^{2}]+4[(y-2)^{2}-{2}^{2}]+25 & =0 \\\\ [(x+5)^{2}-25]+4[(y-2)^{2}-4]+25 & =0 \\\\ (x+5)^{2}-25+4(y-2)^{2}-16+25 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rearrange the equation into the desired form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+5)^{2}-25+4(y-2)^{2}-16+25 & =0 \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+4(y-2)^{2} & =25-25+16 \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+4(y-2)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{(x+5)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+5)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $4>2,$ the length of the major axis is $2\\cdot 4=8.$",
